Started this game quite a while ago, finally got around to finishing it.
This was my first character to reach Gehennom since I intalled Heck^2, and I
must say I quite enjoy it.  I only got a few of the levels, mostly ones that
had small rooms in various parts of the mazes.  It really broke things up,
made things more interesting.  Oh, and I stumbled into Demogorgan in his new
home lair, that was... exciting.

Just a couple of close calls in this game.  The Cromatic dragon hits HARD.
She almost killed me, but I chased her up the stairs of her lair so I could
heal in peace.  The next close call was in Asmodeus's lair, I decided that I
wanted a unique pet, so I did the magic trap dance.  He gated in Baalzebub,
who in turn gated in Greyon.  Once all three were there, I noticed that my
HP was dropping too quickly, so I quaffed a c!oGL.  Ended up killing all
three of them, since I'd spent so much time already trying to kill them.
The last close call was in the scantum, after dispatching the priest, and a
wizard, I was fighting the other when  I realized that my hp was dangerously
low again.  This I noticed just as I finished off the last wizard.  Then I
noticed that most of the summoned monsters outside the scantum were averse
to crossing the traps to come in, so I was able to heal a bit before moving
up (another c!oGL)

The planes were a cakewalk, Air was a bit tricky but I just ran accross the
bottom, and only had to fight a couple of the air elementals of doom.
Astral was fairly easy, I'm pretty sure I should have taken a longer walk,
but I figured why risk a sure thing

